  "body": "Part of #4245 (the CAM-first workspace plan), step 0, PR K. It merges after PR R (the split of `panes.rs`).\n\n## What happens\n\nThe theme tokens, the theme-file reader and the contrast checks are in `crates/ui`. The maintainer asked on Discord to collect the UI/UX work into a crate, and answered on #4245 (2026-11-27): \"one crate for the design system only (tokens, theme and components)\"; the panes stay in `crates/ui`.\n\n## Expected\n\n- A new crate `crates/ui-kit` (`camcraft-ui-kit`). It depends on `egui` only, not on `camcraft-app` or any engine crate.\n- Move the theme tokens, the theme-file reader and the contrast checks into it. `crates/ui` keeps the old module paths as re-exports in this PR, so that no other code changes. Later PRs move components into the kit, each in the PR that touches the component.\n- A small gallery binary in the kit shows each token and theme (light and dark). Later PRs add their components to it.\n- A decision entry in `docs/decisions/` for the new crate edge `ui → ui-kit` (AGENTS.md \"No new dependency between our crates without a decision\"): the imported items, why the caller cannot pass the values in, and what rebuilds when the kit changes.\n- The visual language follows the maintainer's rules on #4245: flat panes with hairlines, no shadows or cards, small radii, structure from type, compact rows. Our own token names and values; nothing from the SolidCraft kit (#655 stays `P?`).\n\n## Done means\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui-kit` runs without building flecs or the engine.\n- The contrast tests run in the kit. `crates/ui` tests pass unchanged; the `crates/ui` test count does not go down.\n- The gallery binary builds and shows the tokens in both themes.\n- The decision entry exists.\n\nEffort: high (a new crate, a workspace change, the decision entry). The maintainer merges it (a new crate edge and a workspace manifest change).\n",
